    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1006">

                <pb facs="0878" n="762" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg762"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/3389.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-26T21:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 26, 1912—9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The press censorship is rigid, and it is evident that consular telegrams are
                    being refused upon some pretext. I receive no reports from consuls either on
                    Pacific coast or the south.</p>
                <p>Acting on consular reports from Tampico I have directly requested the governor of
                    San Luis Potosí to protect Americans and have his telegram in agreement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
